    "upstream_operation": "HMAC 2.0 AFT (MAC generation: key + msg -> mac, truncated to macLen bits) — one upstream file per digest; each testGroup names its own upstream file (source_path/source_sha256)",
    "local_operation": "C_SignInit(CKM_<hash>_HMAC_GENERAL, CK_MAC_GENERAL_PARAMS = macLen/8) + C_Sign, output byte-compared to mac; then C_VerifyInit(same) + C_Verify(mac) must return CKR_OK. Product-authored negatives (bit-flipped MAC, one-byte-short MAC) are derived at run time and labelled product-authored, never NIST",
    "transformation": "subset only; every retained field is byte-copied from the upstream files (hex case preserved); groups renumbered by digest but keep their upstream tgId",
    "subset_policy": "Deterministic. Per digest (all 11 HMAC digests both engines advertise), from the single upstream AFT group, excluding tcIds already carried by hmac_test/hmac_sha384_test/hmac_sha512_test: the case with the shortest key, the longest key, the shortest message (0 bytes where present), the longest message, the shortest MAC and the longest MAC, de-duplicated, ties by lowest tcId. The pinned upstream samples register macLen 80..160 bits only, so no full-length (untruncated) HMAC tag and no CKM_<hash>_HMAC (non-general) case exists in them — not claimed.",
    "retained_fields": "tcId, key, keyLen, msg, msgLen, mac, macLen",
    "negative_classes_upstream": "none — HMAC 2.0 AFT has no testPassed=false case; invalid-MAC rows are product-authored mutations"
  },
